# Commercial S12.1 simulator session-identity diagnosis

- Scope: executable Control simulator result-fetch invariant.
- Finding: authenticated fetch checked a triggered reference but did not require
  the same registered session object, allowing scenario substitution in the
  model.
- Correction: result fetch now requires identity membership in the registered
  session map and executes a same-reference/different-object negative journey.
- Runtime effect: none; this tightens source-only validation before freeze.
